<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ensisheim</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ensisheim is a small town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, north of Mulhouse. From the late 15th century until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War it was the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> government of Further <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, with a regency and treasury for the western lands. It is known for the Ensisheim meteorite, which fell in 1492 and is the oldest recorded meteorite fall in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> whose stone survives.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ensisheim.jpg" alt="Ensisheim" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rauenstein · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ensisheim,_Mairie_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
